    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17720" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farrĕus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>made of spelt</i>, or in gen. <i>of corn</i> or
				<i>grain</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">far. vel triticeus panis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					7, 12, 10</span></i>
			: spicum, <i>an ear of corn</i>, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 280, 9</span></i> Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farrĕum</span></b> , i, n. (sc.
			libum), <i>a speltcake</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 3,
				3, § 10</span></i>.</div>
